# Stitch Skills (Cotarco)

Official docs: get-started, roundtrip, build-in-a-loop, taste, design-md, reference on stitch.withgoogle.com/docs.

Repo skills (`.agents/skills/`): `stitch-design`, `enhance-prompt`, `design-md`, `taste-design`, `stitch-loop`.

## Mandatory pipeline before Stitch / structural UI

Follow `cotarco-commercial-manager/agents.md` §5.2:

1. UI Skills MCP selection (§5.1)
2. Ensure `.stitch/DESIGN.md` exists — `taste-design` (Cotarco brand) or `design-md` from an existing screen
3. `enhance-prompt` including DESIGN.md Section 6
4. Stitch MCP via `stitch-design` (max 3 refine cycles per screen)
5. Stage under `.stitch/designs/`; update `.stitch/SITE.md` + `.stitch/metadata.json`
6. Multi-screen: `stitch-loop` baton (`.stitch/next-prompt.md`)
7. After visual QA only: frontend implementation (`04-frontend`)

## Hard rules

- Do not call Stitch without a useful `.stitch/DESIGN.md`
- Cotarco brand wins: `#FF3C1D`, `#6B6363`, `#FFFFFF`, `#000000`
- Do not treat Stitch HTML as final Next.js code
- Do not write stitch-loop output into `frontend/` or invent `site/public/`
- Handoff must include `STITCH_SKILLS_USED` and `UI_SKILLS_SELECTED`
